.TH MECHANISM 2
.SH NAME
mechanism \- live articulated dynamical-model interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B include "danby/mechanism.m";
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Mechanism
separates a model's ODE state from its depiction.  A model supplies derivatives,
parameter bounds, an array of Cartesian points, link index pairs, and two
observable quantities.  The shared client integrates the state, draws the linked
geometry with automatic scaling, and plots both quantities against time.
.PP
This representation is reusable for human motion, pendulums, springs, linkages,
and other systems where a trajectory alone does not explain the dynamics.
.SH SOURCE
.B /module/danby/mechanism.m
.br
.B /appl/temple/mechanism.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR numerics (2),
.IR plot (2)
